; A rule of characters whose class starts above the Latin-1 range, so that the parser has to decode a sequence
; (a class that holds every byte from 0x80 is matched without decoding: CONTEXTS section 26, item 21).  Only the shortest
; form of a scalar value is UTF-8 (no overlong form, no surrogate, nothing past U+10FFFF); the others are not text
; (CONTEXTS section 26, item 21).
prefix none
whitespace none
doc = 1*cp
cp = 0x20..0x7E / 0x100..0x10FFFF
